--TEST--
an object Core\Storage::get reads back is `tainted bytes`, so it cannot become plain text without a launderer, and the keys Core\Storage::list answers stay plain — `rule:security/tainted-sources`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A visitor's upload is usually what put the object on the disk.
bytes $plain = Core\Storage::get("files", "note.txt") ?? "" as bytes;
string $text = (Core\Storage::get("files", "note.txt") ?? "" as bytes) as string;

// A key is letters, digits, `.`, `-` and `_`, so it compiles as a plain string.
array<string> $keys = Core\Storage::list("files");
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `bytes`, found `bytes|tainted bytes`
  --> case.nvs:3:16
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:4:16
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
